# Architecture Principles

Guide stack rule generation toward explicit, testable, well-separated architectures.

## Core Philosophy

PhilosophyRules {
  ExplicitOverMagic => prefer code you can read without knowing library internals
  PureCore => business logic free of side effects
  SeparatedConcerns => state, UI, effects in distinct modules
  TestabilityFirst => architecture enables easy testing
  StandardOverFramework => vanilla patterns over framework abstractions
}

## Explicit Over Magic

(library hides complexity) => prefer explicit alternative when equally capable
(framework "magic") => understand cost: debugging, onboarding, lock-in

ExplicitGuidance {
  PreferVanilla => standard language/platform features over library abstractions
  VisibleFlow => data and control flow readable in code
  MinimalAbstraction => each layer must justify its existence
}

LifecycleCalibration {
  PoC => magic acceptable for speed
  TeamTool => explicit preferred, magic acceptable if well-understood
  MVP+ => explicit required for core, magic acceptable at edges
  MatureProduction => explicit throughout, minimal dependencies
}

## Separation of Concerns

SeparationLayers {
  State => data and transitions, no UI, no IO
  UI => presentation only, receives data and callbacks
  Effects => IO, network, side effects isolated
  Logic => pure functions, deterministic, testable
}

(concern mixing detected) => suggest separation
(UI contains business logic) => extract to pure functions
(state management contains IO) => isolate effects

### Patterns by Domain

StateSeparation {
  Pattern => "state transitions via pure functions"
  Test => "input state + action → output state"
}

EffectSeparation {
  Pattern => "describe effects, don't execute inline"
  Test => "verify effect descriptions without execution"
}

UISeparation {
  Pattern => "container/presentation or equivalent"
  Container => "wires data and actions, no markup"
  Presentation => "pure render from props, no state management"
}

## Pure Core / Imperative Shell

ArchitectureModel {
  Core => pure functions, business logic, deterministic
  Shell => IO, effects, framework integration
  Boundary => thin adapter between core and shell
}

(business logic in shell) => move to core
(IO in core) => move to shell

Benefits {
  Testability => core tested without mocks
  Portability => core framework-agnostic
  Reasoning => pure functions easier to understand
}

## Testability-First Architecture

TestabilityRules {
  PublicAPI => test through public interfaces, not internals
  Deterministic => same input → same output
  Isolation => no shared mutable state between tests
  NoMocks => architecture that minimizes mocking needs
}

(requires extensive mocking) => suggests poor separation
(test touches internals) => suggests leaky abstraction

TestPatterns {
  StateLogic => "set up via actions, assert via selectors"
  PureFunctions => "input → output, no setup needed"
  Effects => "verify descriptions, not execution"
  Integration => "thin layer at boundaries only"
}

## Standard Over Framework

FrameworkGuidance {
  Evaluate => "what does this abstract? could I write it?"
  Prefer => "libraries over frameworks, functions over classes"
  Avoid => "deep lock-in, framework-specific patterns throughout"
}

(framework pattern) => ensure team understands underlying concept
(multiple framework options) => prefer less magical, more explicit

LifecycleCalibration {
  PoC => use whatever ships fastest
  TeamTool => prefer understandable over powerful
  MVP => balance productivity with explicitness
  Production => explicit, minimal dependencies, long-term maintainability
}

## Code Generation Philosophy

When generating code or guiding AI to generate code:

GenerationRules {
  HighLevelSpec => generate explicit implementation
  AbstractionDirection => specs more abstract than output
  Transparency => generated code readable without generator knowledge
}

(generated code) => should be maintainable without regeneration
(spec language) => higher level than target language

## Lifecycle Calibration Matrix

| Principle | PoC | TeamTool | MVP | Production |
|-----------|-----|----------|-----|------------|
| Explicit over magic | Low | Medium | High | Required |
| Separation | Minimal | Moderate | Good | Strict |
| Pure core | Optional | Encouraged | Required | Required |
| Testability | Manual OK | Critical paths | Comprehensive | Thorough |
| Standard over framework | Speed first | Understandable | Balanced | Minimal deps |

Constraints {
  Architecture should enable testing, not require heroics.
  Prefer boring, explicit code over clever abstractions.
  Each layer of indirection must justify its cost.
  Generated code should be readable standalone.
}
